claim.claim-text:
a pump mechanism (42) for dispensing fluid (60) from the fluid dispenser (10);
a light emitter (118);
a light sensor (120); and
a movable component that moves when the pump mechanism (42) is activated;
the method comprising:

emitting light from the light emitter (118);
detecting movement of the movable component using the light sensor (120) by detecting changes in an amount of the light emitted by the light emitter (118) that is reflected from the movable component towards the light sensor (120); and
determining whether the pump mechanism (42) has been activated based on detection data received from the light sensor (120).

wherein the pump position sensor (94) comprises a first magnet sensor (104) that is oriented in a first orientation and a second magnet sensor (106) that is oriented in a second orientation, the first orientation being different than the second orientation;
the method further comprising detecting a position of the magnet (102) over time using the first magnet sensor (104) and the second magnet sensor (106); and
wherein determining the position of the pump mechanism (42) over time comprises determining the position of the pump mechanism (42) over time based on the sensor data from the first magnet sensor (104) and the second magnet sensor (106).

activating the data communication device (90) when the pump mechanism (42) has been activated; and
setting the threshold volume or updating the threshold volume based on user data received by the data communication device (90) from the mobile communication device;
wherein the fluid dispenser (10) is a hand cleaning fluid dispenser (10) for dispensing a hand cleaning fluid (60).
